From 3b108561efe075545d4e5f1e4ed67db37af539ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 13:57:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): correct verified CLI-command inaccuracies in
 skill bodies
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follows the description+evals pass in this PR with body corrections, each
verified against the live forge CLI / source (not the agents' first-pass
claims, which contained cross-skill contradictions):

- issue-basics: `feature` is NOT a canonical issue type — the kernel's four
  types are task/bug/epic/decision (issue-command-contract.js). `--type` is
  stored verbatim/unvalidated (create --type feature => ok:true), and epics/
  decisions are excluded from the ready queue by convention, not enforced at
  claim time (claim <epic> => ok:true). Fixed the type lists, example, and notes.
- triage-ready: stats `data.counts` has no `in_progress` bucket (keys are
  open/done/cancelled; claimed work stays `open`, surfaced via active_claims);
  there is no `claimable` field in the CLI JSON.
- kernel: `forge remember`/`forge recall` are LIVE (were mislabeled "planned");
  only `forge knowledge search` is not on the CLI yet.
- hermes-forge: orient sections carry no per-section `priority` field — trim
  order is `token_budget.truncation_order`; bare `forge recap --json` requires an
  issue id (errors without one), it does not return a legacy summary.
- plan: `forge issue dep cycles` and `forge graph` are not real commands — use
  `forge issue blocked` / `forge issue children <epic-id>`.
- validate: `bun run check` runs `scripts/validate.js` (not .sh); `forge update`
  takes no `--comment` flag, so split into `forge update --status` + `forge comment`.
- ship/review: `forge update --comment` -> `forge comment` (the real verb).
- verify: `gh pr view --json deployments` is an invalid field -> `statusCheckRollup`.
- sonarcloud: removed a dead reference to a non-existent TS client path.
- rollback: `Rollback:` commit prefix -> `chore: rollback` (matches bin/forge.js).

Deferred (kernel issue 4109f471): the rollback skill's `bd update --status
reverted` path — a Beads/kernel migration decision, not a doc edit. .codex mirror
regenerated (inSync); skill tests green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
